\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Theorem}
\title{Translation covariance and the fixed-background criterion}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For the \vocabk{cochain and link translations}{fdip-00W0}
with any finite free coefficient representation,
##{\begin{aligned}
\tau_a\extD_U\tau_a^{-1}&=\extD_{\tau_a U},\\
\tau_a\cov_U\tau_a^{-1}&=\cov_{\tau_a U}.
\end{aligned}}
For either choice of operator, the translation commutes with it
exactly when it has
\vocabk{represented-link invariance}{fdip-00W0}.
If #{\rho} is faithful, this is equivalent to
#{\tau_a U=U}. The criterion holds also at
periods #{1} and #{2}.}

\proof{
\p{Substitution in the forward and inverse pullbacks
gives
##{\begin{aligned}
(\tau_a T_i^U\tau_a^{-1}f)(x)
 &=\rho(U_i(x+a))^{-1}f(x+\varepsilon_i),\\
(\tau_a(T_i^U)^{-1}\tau_a^{-1}f)(x)
 &=\rho(U_i(x+a-\varepsilon_i))f(x-\varepsilon_i).
\end{aligned}}
These are the pullbacks for #{\tau_a U}. The
exterior operators commute with #{\tau_a}, giving
##{\begin{aligned}
\tau_a\extd_U\tau_a^{-1}&=\extd_{\tau_a U},\\
\tau_a\extdag_U\tau_a^{-1}&=\extdag_{\tau_a U}.
\end{aligned}}
Their sum and their difference therefore transform as stated.
Equality of represented links preserves each pullback and hence
each of these operators.}

\p{Conversely, suppose translation preserves the chosen operator.
Restrict to a degree-zero input and take the degree-one
coefficient along #{e_i} at #{x}. The contractions
vanish, leaving the difference of the two
forward pullbacks. A function supported at
#{x+\varepsilon_i} can take any value #{z\in F}
there, so
##{\rho(U_i(x+a))^{-1}z=\rho(U_i(x))^{-1}z}
for every #{z}. The two endomorphisms are equal,
and so are their inverses. This proves
represented-link invariance. At period one the
input site equals #{x}; the identical identity
subtractions still cancel. At period two the
argument still reads the labeled forward
transport, so it does not merge the two positive
links. Faithfulness gives the final literal-link
criterion.}
}
